        "The gameplay flush calls factory 0x005DD240, whose allocation path calls constructor 0x005E3690 and installs vtable 0x00F2FF80; the flush transfers the exact +0x150 list pointer into outer +0x18, clears the source pointer, and passes the outer object to 0x00A8D500. When A8D500 sees [this+0x10] nonzero, its ready branch enqueues the object; the refusal branch releases it through vtable +0x04. Both branches return zero and the flush caller ignores EAX. The successful runtime ID is 0x6E6F.",
        "PROVEN_EXACT_STATIC_SUCCESS_PATH", "0x6E6F",
        "PROVEN_EXACT_STATIC_SUCCESS_PATH", "UNKNOWN", "NOT_ESTABLISHED_BY_IMAGE",
        "gameplay", ("gameplay_factory", "transfer", "runtime_ctor", "runtime_reg", "runtime_getter", "transport_enqueue"),
        "gameplay outer factory, construction, ownership transfer, and conditional transport acceptance",
        "Static control flow does not prove every live click reaches this branch, that A8D500 accepts the outer object in every live state, or that 0x6E6F is a top-level packet opcode.",
